
=== License Key

The web console requires a valid license key before it will allow access to screens.
The user is prompted automatically to enter a valid license key if one is missing.
The license key can also be updated from the Configure License screen.

License Info:: A description of the license type.
Holder:: The company name or email address of the license holder.
Effective Date:: Date and time when the license will become valid.
Expiration Date:: Date and time when the license will no longer be valid.
Max Maintenance:: The end date and time for maintenance and support.  Defaults to expiration date if not present.
Max Nodes:: The maximum number of nodes that can be created for synchronization.
Max Groups:: The maximum number of node groups that can be created for synchronization.
Max Tables:: The maximum number of table triggers that can be created for synchronization. A trigger only counts toward the limit when it has a corresponding trigger router and sync on insert, update, or delete is enabled. Multiple triggers with the same source table name (case insensitive) are counted as one trigger.
Max Rows:: The maximum number of rows that can be synchronized in a 24-hour period.
Job Schedule In Seconds:: The minimum allowed interval in seconds between Push, Pull, and custom job executions. Jobs configured to run more frequently than this limit will use this interval instead.
Mobile Multiplier:: A multiplier applied to node limits for mobile nodes. The max nodes limit is multiplied by this value to determine the allowed number of mobile nodes.
Compare Repair:: Indicates whether the compare and repair feature is enabled. When enabled, data can be compared between source and target nodes and optionally repaired to resolve differences.
Jumpmind Access Token Required:: Indicates whether the root node must obtain and maintain a valid access token from Jumpmind. When enabled, the root node requests an access token from Jumpmind when it starts and periodically refreshes it.
Instance ID:: If present in the license key, this unique identifier must match the installation. If not present, the instance ID for the current installation is shown in parentheses.
 

The license key is a block of encoded text that is sent to the user over email, or it can be retrieved from the
http://support.jumpmind.com/[Support Center].  When an installed license key expires, the web console
will require a new valid key before allowing access, but data synchronization and command line access
will continue to function normally.

